Patch 23: reduce the two-pass dry pass to the tools that actually rank shapes.

Standalone, against anchor 5d628d8 (current origin/av2-enc). Three independent
changes to the DryPassCfg initialiser in av2_rd_pick_inter_mode_sb, each behind
its own build-time switch so the arm decomposes by rebuild rather than by patch
edit.

VERIFICATION STATUS: confirmed to change the encode. On a 192x128 2-frame clip
at cpu-used=4 the bitstream md5 differs from baseline (615ff9e8... vs
c2a7fb30..., 6985 vs 6996 bytes). Local runtime was flat, but that clip is one
key frame plus one inter frame and two-pass is inter-only, so the key frame
dominates the measurement. The magnitude needs CTC.

WHY THE DRY PASS. The two-pass superblock partition search (#5253) added a
first "dry" pass whose stated job is to "work out a rough partition shape ...
because it only has to rank shapes against each other, not produce the final
coding decision". Its tool reduction is expressed as a DryPassCfg struct with
about eighteen hard-coded caps. Nothing in this project has ever tuned them,
and three of them are doing more work than ranking requires.

(1) WARP MODES. cfg->motion_mode_mask restricts the dry pass to
SIMPLE_TRANSLATION, but a few hundred lines below there is an escape hatch:

    if (base_mbmi.mode == WARPMV || base_mbmi.mode == WARP_NEWMV) {
      modes_to_search = allowed_motion_modes;     // full set
    } else if (x->apply_dry_pass_shortcuts) {
      modes_to_search = cfg->motion_mode_mask;    // SIMPLE_TRANSLATION
    }

The bypass is correct on its own terms -- WARPMV asserts motion_mode ==
WARP_DELTA, so restricting it would produce an invalid prediction -- but it
means these two modes are the only ones in the dry pass running the FULL motion
mode set, including WARP_DELTA and its nested trial loops. Every other mode
gets a single translation trial. The dry pass's most expensive inner loops
belong to the two modes its own reduction cannot reach. Removing them from
inter_mode_mask closes the hatch from the other side.

(2) MV PRECISION 3 -> 1. Each extra precision re-runs the motion search at a
finer step, shifting the MV cost of every candidate shape in the same
direction, so the shape ranking is largely invariant to it.

(3) WEDGE DROPPED. Wedge search partitions a block into two soft-bounded
regions -- itself a shape decision, evaluated inside a pass whose only job is
choosing the block shape, and the partition shapes being ranked already express
that split. It is also the expensive member of the mask.

In all three cases the wet pass still runs the full tool on the surviving
shape, so what is given up is ranking fidelity, not final coding quality. That
is the trade the dry pass was built to make; these changes take it further in
the direction it already chose.

Switches, all defaulting to the new behaviour:

    -DAVM_DRY_PASS_WARP_MODES=1    restore warp modes
    -DAVM_DRY_PASS_PRECISIONS=3    restore three precisions
    -DAVM_DRY_PASS_WEDGE=1         restore wedge

Setting all three restores the current encoder exactly, which makes both the
fallback and the per-change attribution free.

diff --git a/av2/encoder/rdopt.c b/av2/encoder/rdopt.c
index c6d5434..5c8169a 100644
--- a/av2/encoder/rdopt.c
+++ b/av2/encoder/rdopt.c
@@ -9166,11 +9166,66 @@ void av2_rd_pick_inter_mode_sb(struct AV2_COMP *cpi,
       .intra_fsc_cap = 0,
       .intra_mrl_cap = 0,
       .motion_mode_mask = (1u << SIMPLE_TRANSLATION),
-      .compound_type_mask = (1u << COMPOUND_AVERAGE) | (1u << COMPOUND_WEDGE),
+      // (3) Wedge dropped from the dry pass. Wedge search partitions a block
+      // into two regions with a soft boundary -- itself a shape decision, made
+      // inside a pass whose only job is choosing the block shape. The partition
+      // shapes being ranked already express the same directional split. Wedge
+      // is also the expensive member of the mask, iterating wedge indices with
+      // a compound-type RD per candidate where COMPOUND_AVERAGE is one blend.
+      // The wet pass still searches wedge on the winning shape.
+#ifndef AVM_DRY_PASS_WEDGE
+#define AVM_DRY_PASS_WEDGE 0
+#endif
+      .compound_type_mask = (1u << COMPOUND_AVERAGE)
+#if AVM_DRY_PASS_WEDGE
+                            | (1u << COMPOUND_WEDGE)
+#endif
+      ,
+      // (1) Warp prediction modes excluded from the dry pass.
+      //
+      // The dry pass reduces motion modes to SIMPLE_TRANSLATION through
+      // cfg->motion_mode_mask, but that reduction has an escape hatch:
+      //
+      //   if (base_mbmi.mode == WARPMV || base_mbmi.mode == WARP_NEWMV) {
+      //     modes_to_search = allowed_motion_modes;     // full set
+      //   } else if (x->apply_dry_pass_shortcuts) {
+      //     modes_to_search = cfg->motion_mode_mask;    // SIMPLE_TRANSLATION
+      //   }
+      //
+      // The bypass is correct on its own terms: WARPMV asserts
+      // motion_mode == WARP_DELTA, so forcing SIMPLE_TRANSLATION would give an
+      // invalid prediction. The consequence is that these two modes are the
+      // only ones in the dry pass that run the FULL motion mode set, including
+      // WARP_DELTA and its nested trial loops -- warp_ref_idx x
+      // warp_precision_idx for WARP_NEWMV, warp_ref_idx x warpmv_with_mvd_flag
+      // x warp_inter_intra for WARPMV. Every other mode gets a single trial.
+      // The dry pass's most expensive inner loops belong to the two modes its
+      // own tool reduction cannot reach; this closes the hatch from the other
+      // side.
+      //
+      // The dry pass ranks partition shapes rather than producing a coding
+      // decision. Warp refines the motion MODEL within a shape and improves
+      // prediction roughly uniformly across the shapes being compared, so the
+      // shape winning under warp is very likely the one winning under
+      // translation. The wet pass still searches warp on the surviving shape.
+#ifndef AVM_DRY_PASS_WARP_MODES
+#define AVM_DRY_PASS_WARP_MODES 0
+#endif
       .inter_mode_mask = (1u << NEWMV) | (1u << NEW_NEWMV) | (1u << NEARMV) |
-                         (1u << NEAR_NEARMV) | (1u << WARPMV) |
-                         (1u << WARP_NEWMV),
-      .precisions_from_top = 3,
+                         (1u << NEAR_NEARMV)
+#if AVM_DRY_PASS_WARP_MODES
+                         | (1u << WARPMV) | (1u << WARP_NEWMV)
+#endif
+      ,
+      // (2) One MV precision instead of three. Precision refinement is a
+      // within-shape refinement: each extra precision re-runs motion search at
+      // a finer step and shifts the MV cost of every candidate shape in the
+      // same direction, so the ranking is largely invariant to it. The wet pass
+      // still searches the full precision ladder on the surviving shape.
+#ifndef AVM_DRY_PASS_PRECISIONS
+#define AVM_DRY_PASS_PRECISIONS 1
+#endif
+      .precisions_from_top = AVM_DRY_PASS_PRECISIONS,
       .intra_mpm_cap = 13,
     };
     // Keep the normal distortion measure; a cheaper one made the partition
